<title>UK: NAB adds A$100 million to seven-year bond.</title>
<headline>NAB adds A$100 million to seven-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to A$200 million from A$100 million, lead manager Hambros Bank said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NATIONAL AUSTRALIA BANK</p>
<p> AMT  * A$200	   COUPON     7.00	MATURITY    23.JUL.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.495   PAY DATE    23.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> NOTES   *  ORIGINAL A$100 MLN LAUNCHED 12 JUNE AT 101.01</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/GB/AU</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC  1.50	PRAECIPUUM  0.125</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF MTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
